# hermes-roam 0.5.0 — full demo run under real Hermes 0.22.5 (sanitized log)
#
# scripts/demo-two-homes.sh /tmp/roam-demo-050b — exit code 0.
# Stages: 1 local backend (push/pull, secrets, conflicts, deletions, shared
# config keys, per-device rules.yaml), 2 git backend round trip, 3 history +
# restore, 4 the 0.4.1 opt-in session archive on a fresh local pair
# (nothing travels with the opt-in off; an opted-in push publishes; the peer
# pulls the archive read-only (0444), lists and prints it; a device that
# never opts in never publishes its own sessions; roam status shows the
# opt-ins), 5 the 0.5.0 multi-profile contract on a fresh local pair: a
# REAL `hermes profile create` profile with its own soul, memory, skill and
# config and a real imported per-profile session is pushed by one device
# (the push names the covered root and publishes both profiles'
# transcripts), a brand-new device pulls it (the plan carries the
# brand-new-device notice and the covered root), the profile arrives
# listable with its content, the first-pull config union brings the shared
# model keys into the root AND profile configs while the fresh device's own
# api_key stays, the grouped archive listing shows eps/default and
# eps/work and `sessions show` prints the per-profile transcript, and
# `hermes -p work roam status` maps up to the ROOT home. The demo key and
# the redacted api_key markers are placeholders; no secret is printed.
# Every 'verified:' line marks an assertion that passed; there are no FAIL
# lines.



